{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]The kingdom is like treasure [Eb]in the field
[F]A man found it and [Bb]hid it again [F/A]
[Gm]In his joy he went and [Eb]sold his all
[Cm]To buy the [Bb]field where the treasure [Fsus4]lay [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]He sold ev[Dm]erything he [Eb]had
For the [F]pearl of great value
[Bb]The merchant found [Dm]one precious [Eb]stone
And [F]gave his life for [Bb]it [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]A net let down into the deep [Eb]sea
[F]Caught fish of every kind and [Bb]sort [F/A]
[Gm]They hauled it up upon [Eb]the shore
[Cm]And sat to [Bb]sort the good from [F]bad
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]He sold ev[Dm]erything he [Eb]had
